WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.707
Thanks to Google Meet
for sponsoring a portion of today's video.

00:00:09.719 --> 00:00:11.115
It's been so many years.

00:00:13.226 --> 00:00:14.866
Long have I waited.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.417
Finally, it's my turn.

00:00:23.284 --> 00:00:24.481
Hello Internet.

00:00:24.481 --> 00:00:29.500
Welcome to Film Theory, the show
that always knew that this day was coming.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.630
It's been over eight years, but finally,
the 5 minutes of Freddy's live

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:36.370
action feature film is set to hit the
silver screen in a little over a month.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:37.980
And you know what that means.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:41.260
It means that nowhere is safe anymore
from FNAF theories.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.260
Don't believe me?

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:45.570
There's a FNAF cookbook
releasing in October, a FNAF cookbook.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.010
It's coming for you next, Food Theory.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:50.140
Now all we need is a FNAF fashion line
that's infected all of us.

00:00:50.919 --> 00:00:51.802
Oh, my sweet stars.

00:00:51.802 --> 00:00:52.860
What have I done?

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:54.229
But for a satisfying

00:00:54.229 --> 00:00:56.079
as it is for Film Theory
to take another toy

00:00:56.079 --> 00:00:58.449
out of the toy box of Game
Theory and claim it is our own -

00:00:58.449 --> 00:01:01.809
see also Sonic, Mario
and Last of Us in this year alone -

00:01:01.809 --> 00:01:04.900
In all seriousness,
we are way overdue for a theory

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.810
breaking down our predictions
for this movie.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:09.880
And believe me,
there is plenty to talk about.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:11.690
If you're on YouTube
and you somehow missed the phenomenon

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:13.840
that is Five Nights at Freddy's, how?

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:14.840
Genuinely, how?

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.310
I need to know your secrets.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:20.290
This series exploded about a decade ago
with every let's player on the platform

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:22.760
screaming their heads off
over the haunted animatronics

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:25.140
hunting us down in the ruins
of a dilapidated pizzeria.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:29.430
But while the scare certainly got us started,
it's the story that's kept us going.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:31.390
What's helped the series persist
for as long as it has

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:33.049
has been its incredibly mysterious story

00:01:33.049 --> 00:01:36.600
told through scraps of information
and obscure environmental details.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.940
Heck, 60 episodes later on Game Theory

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.170
and we are still trying
to decode this thing.

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:42.410
Really, it's only been 60?

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:44.330
It feels like
it's got to be 100 at this point.

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:47.540
And this new FNAF movie seems to be
staying true to the franchise's roots,

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.320
not in terms of the lore necessarily,
but in terms of the cryptic storytelling.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:55.350
There is a ton of information packed into
the few short minutes of trailer footage

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:56.829
that we've seen so far, enough

00:01:56.829 --> 00:02:00.130
that I believe we can predict
the entire plot of this new movie

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:03.189
right down to the shocking twist ending
that's going to leave you devastated.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.240
Here's a hint: if you think this movie has
itself

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:06.710
a happy ending with everyone smiling

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:10.500
and living happily ever after, then clearly
you have not been paying attention.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:15.580
So today, Film Theory does what Game
Theory's never been able to do: solve

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.250
this franchise.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:20.170
And we're going to do it
before the movie even releases.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:22.480
Keep your eyes on your monitors, loyal
theorists,

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:23.480
we're going in.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:24.590
So we think a good place to start with

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:26.280
our prediction here is sort of laying out

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:29.660
what we think the movie's trying to do
with FNAF as a franchise.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:31.190
Just from watching these trailers,
I think it's clear

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:34.310
that this movie does not take place
in the universe of the games.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:35.419
Why? This thing.

00:02:35.419 --> 00:02:38.100
I have played, watched
and read every last scrap of information

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:42.280
this franchise has put out, and this is
unlike anything we've ever seen before.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:45.960
Clearly, it's a murder weapon, and clearly
it was made by the franchise's big bad.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:47.053
But why? What?

00:02:47.053 --> 00:02:49.120
And how? is still a complete mystery.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:50.819
My best guess, and again
this one is a guess,

00:02:50.819 --> 00:02:52.390
is that it's a remnant extractor,

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:55.200
a way to ensure murder victims
have the most traumatic,

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.209
awful death possible so the agony
they experience can be harvested

00:02:58.209 --> 00:03:00.330
to help create creatures
with eternal life.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:03.480
If none of that meant anything
to you, strap in El Chipo,

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.790
you're in for a crash course.

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:06.880
By the end of this thing,
you're going to be talking about Faz-Goo

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.489
with the confidence of a pro.

00:03:08.489 --> 00:03:10.870
Looking at the trailers and IMDB,
we know that this is going to be

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:13.470
the story of Mike Schmidt,
a security guard from FNAF 1.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:16.150
But things are different this time around.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:18.410
While this certainly appears
to take place in the 1990s

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:21.180
like the original FNAF game,
considering everyone's using old school

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:25.599
wired telephones, there are no modern cars
and all the monitors are old CRTs,

00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:28.650
they're also bringing in characters
who clearly reference later parts

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:32.569
of the franchise, specifically Vanessa
from Security Breach, a blond security

00:03:32.569 --> 00:03:35.540
guard in the game who here appears
as a blond police officer.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:37.860
What I think's going on here
from a meta perspective

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.580
is that the movie is taking
a bunch of stories from the game franchise

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:43.689
and simplifying them for a general film
audience while trying to keep

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:45.730
the most iconic aspects of the games
intact.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:47.780
Plus, they're going to be combining ideas
and characters

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:49.251
from different areas of the franchise

00:03:49.251 --> 00:03:52.819
to get as many recognizable aspects
of FNAF into one film as possible.

00:03:52.819 --> 00:03:53.879
That's why we see the story

00:03:53.879 --> 00:03:57.010
from the original FNAF interacting
with someone new from Security Breach.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:58.849
And then you have a girl
named Abby mixed in there

00:03:58.849 --> 00:04:01.090
whose name is literally
an anagram of baby,

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:04.260
all fighting against an unbroken version
of Spring Trap.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.170
That right there,
that is the filmmakers trying to bridge

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:09.382
the gap between the different eras of FNAF
and bring in as many fans as they can.

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:11.349
The OGs from 2014,

00:04:11.349 --> 00:04:14.379
the new fans from Security Breach,
and also your average Joes who can't

00:04:14.379 --> 00:04:17.979
tell a Fredbear from a Nedd Bear,
let alone a Glamrock from a Rockstar.

00:04:17.979 --> 00:04:19.739
Oh, you have so much to learn.

00:04:19.739 --> 00:04:20.739
So, all in all,

00:04:20.739 --> 00:04:22.190
think of this movie
as something that's going to wipe

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:25.509
the slate clean and start fresh,
referencing moments and key characters

00:04:25.509 --> 00:04:28.400
from the game and books,
but not being beholden to them.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.080
Because, you know,
that's not a confusing route to go at all.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.860
That said, let's just hope
they don't stray too far from the games.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.990
Case in point, this detail right here.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:37.430
During a spoopy, scary moment

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:40.400
in the trailer, Nebraska is spelled out
very clearly on a poster

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:44.289
in very large, very bold letters right
next to the main character's head.

00:04:44.289 --> 00:04:47.110
This was an intentional decision,
definitely put into the trailers

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:48.160
to keep us talking.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.360
This means something.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:53.350
Now, the general consensus is that
the FNAF games normally take place in Utah.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:56.010
Multiple spinoff book series
have made that detail quite clear.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:59.780
Could it be then that they've moved
the setting to Nebraska for some reason?

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:01.160
Maybe, but I don't think so.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:04.060
It'd be weird to just have a state poster
of the state that you're currently in

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:05.750
right above your security desk.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:08.910
My guess is that this poster was put here
intentionally by Mike.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.509
It's important him for some reason.

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:14.480
My best guess is that it's hashtag goals,
an aspirational place to go to to help him

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.050
get out of his current situation.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:18.830
Because on the face of it, things don't
seem to be going all that great for him.

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:21.539
It looks to me like Mike and his family
have fallen on some hard times.

00:05:21.539 --> 00:05:24.280
First off, we don't see his parents
in these trailers at all.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.080
Though Mike's father has been cast,

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:28.449
I'm going to guess
that he's only here for a flashback scene,

00:05:28.449 --> 00:05:31.169
considering he doesn't look too much
older than Mike's actor, Josh Hutcherson.

00:05:31.169 --> 00:05:33.150
Additionally,
we see that Mike and his little sister,

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:36.300
Abby, are living in a small house
with an average car, and Mike is looking

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.873
for any job that he can get.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:44.430
We later see Mike bring in Abby
along with him while he's

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:46.570
working, implying
that this is probably their only option.

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:47.819
They can't afford a babysitter,

00:05:47.819 --> 00:05:49.770
and if there were parents at home
to take care of Abby,

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:52.230
why would he be bringing her
to his nightshift job?

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:56.330
So Nebraska might be a symbolic place
of freedom for Mike, a place to escape

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:57.760
and finally be free.

00:05:57.760 --> 00:05:59.500
More or less, though,
I believe that the setup for the back

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:02.180
story of the FNAF movie is going to align
with that of the first game.

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:03.180
Freddy Fazbear's

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:05.950
Pizzeria was a popular arcade
and food chain represented by its four

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:07.278
iconic mascots.

00:06:11.302 --> 00:06:13.300
However, they're not the only ones here.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.830
It seems that some of the children
encountered

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:18.990
another animatronic, a large yellow bunny
rabbit that's separate from the other four,

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:21.919
as we see in a drawing here on the wall
from this shot.

00:06:21.919 --> 00:06:22.919
This was a costume

00:06:22.919 --> 00:06:25.610
used by the owner of the establishment,
William Afton, an outfit

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:27.580
that he would use
to get closer to the kids,

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:30.419
which honestly is creepier in a movie
than it was in the games.

00:06:30.419 --> 00:06:33.630
You know, just your typical yellow
bunny friend holding hands with five kids,

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:35.780
which when you're talking in horror
movie speak is code

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:37.010
for: he killed those kids,

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:39.729
stuffed them into suits, and eventually
turned them into haunted robots.

00:06:39.729 --> 00:06:41.699
Also, just to call it out here,
I originally thought

00:06:41.699 --> 00:06:42.699
that there was going to be

00:06:42.699 --> 00:06:45.430
something hidden in this wall of drawings
beyond just the obvious.

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:48.660
I mean, it is the perfect spot
to sneak in little bits of hidden lore,

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:50.770
but the more that we've seen of the wall
in other trailers,

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:53.412
there doesn't actually seem
to be that much of anything here, sadly.

00:06:53.412 --> 00:06:55.389
And honestly, surprisingly,
considering the franchise

00:06:55.389 --> 00:06:56.389
we're talking about.

00:06:56.389 --> 00:06:57.389
Speaking of yellow bunny-men,

00:06:57.389 --> 00:06:58.389
the trailer seemed

00:06:58.389 --> 00:07:00.870
determined to convince us that the person
we expected to play the franchise's

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:03.349
big bad isn't
actually playing the villain.

00:07:03.349 --> 00:07:04.960
Despite rumors
that he would be playing our resident

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:07.990
'urple murder man, William
Afton, in the trailers Lillard's character

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:11.460
is clearly labeled as Steve Raglan, career
counselor.

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:12.460
But here's the rub

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:14.669
If there's one thing we've learned here
in Film Theory over the past decade

00:07:14.669 --> 00:07:18.610
it's that trailers can be manipulated
to create mystery or confuse timelines.

00:07:18.610 --> 00:07:22.220
See also Morbius and Infinity War,
just to name two key examples.

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:25.330
And here I think we're being presented
with the exact same sort of misdirect.

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:29.020
In fact, I'm almost 100% confident that
I can prove it beyond a reasonable doubt.

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:31.840
First, Matthew Lillard confirmed
that he signed a three picture deal

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:33.490
to star in more than one FNAF movie.

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:36.849
And unless Steve Raglan's a new character
that Blumhouse is just really hype

00:07:36.849 --> 00:07:39.380
about, I expect that deal was to play
Afton.

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:41.199
However, far more convincingly,

00:07:41.199 --> 00:07:44.830
we have this scene from the trailer
where a young boy is seen getting kidnaped

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:45.830
in the middle of the woods.

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:47.240
Based on the film's official website,

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:50.240
the synopsis reads that Mike is still,
quote, haunted by the unsolved

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:53.199
disappearance of his younger brother
more than a decade before.

00:07:53.199 --> 00:07:55.770
And we know based on casting
that the brothers name is Garrett.

00:07:55.770 --> 00:07:59.020
Now, the actor playing
this kid, Garrett, is named Lucas Grant.

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:00.259
Hopping over to Instagram, Grant

00:08:00.259 --> 00:08:03.851
commented on a post by Matthew Lillard
saying that it was great to work with him

00:08:03.851 --> 00:08:06.080
and that he's much
nicer than his character.

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:07.080
Now tell me,

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:08.080
why would a young actor

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:11.289
playing a kidnaped boy have any reason
to interact with the career counselor?

00:08:11.289 --> 00:08:12.289
He wouldn't.

00:08:12.289 --> 00:08:15.509
The only way they interact is
if Matthew Lillard, Steve Raglan, William

00:08:15.509 --> 00:08:18.389
Afton, call 'em whatever you want,
was kidnapping that kid.

00:08:18.389 --> 00:08:21.770
In other words, in this movie,
a big final reveal will be

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:24.460
that Matthew Lillard
kidnapped Mike's brother.

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:27.650
This would actually parallel
some key moments from the original novel

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:30.419
where William Afton acts
under a pseudonym, Dave Miller,

00:08:30.419 --> 00:08:33.959
and as the perfectly normal, mundane
job of security guard for an old abandoned

00:08:33.959 --> 00:08:37.705
mall, a job that allows him to supervise
the comings and goings around Freddy's.

00:08:37.705 --> 00:08:39.519
That way,
when kids start poking around, he's

00:08:39.519 --> 00:08:42.959
able to hop into the suit - get it hop
because he's a rabbit - hop into the suit

00:08:42.959 --> 00:08:45.950
and try to scare him away,
just like we see him doing here.

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:46.950
And lastly, in the novels

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:50.490
he also kidnaps a kid prior
to becoming a crazed serial killer.

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:52.817
Honestly, a lot of the details here line up. Now

00:08:52.817 --> 00:08:54.580
before we start jumping from video

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:57.019
to video to keep tabs on Freddy
and the gang with more plot predictions,

00:08:57.019 --> 00:09:00.230
let's take a moment to thank a service
that I bet Mike wishes he had, our sponsor

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:02.680
for this portion of today's video:
Google Meet.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:03.680
I'm going to be honest with you guys,

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.339
when Google reached out to us
wanting to partner

00:09:05.339 --> 00:09:09.600
to talk about their video calling app,
Google Meet, I was definitely surprised.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:11.029
Weird theories about spooky movies?

00:09:11.029 --> 00:09:13.980
Yeah, not exactly the first thing that
pops in my head when I hear the words

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:15.150
"video calling app."

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:17.750
But hey, the more I thought about it,
the more it actually makes a lot of sense.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:20.040
See, we've been using Google Meet
for all of our team Theorist

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.920
meetings for years now,

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:23.540
basically
the entire time we've been a business.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.600
We're mostly a remote company
and Google Meet

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:27.240
is the tool that allows that to happen.

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:30.839
It is quite literally a daily part
of my life with no less than 3 hours a day

00:09:30.839 --> 00:09:32.600
being spent on Google Meet.

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:34.670
It also checks out
because Meet slots into so many

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:38.579
other services that we use every day
with zero extra effort on our end:

00:09:38.579 --> 00:09:40.630
Google Docs, Calendar, Gmail, YouTube;

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:42.459
it just works seamlessly.

00:09:42.459 --> 00:09:45.380
Honestly, we have tried other services,
and I hate them.

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:46.550
They're just not as good.

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:49.510
Meet supports one on one calls, obviously,
but it can also invite hundreds

00:09:49.510 --> 00:09:50.510
of participants

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:52.050
if I need everyone in the company

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:54.920
as well as all my extended friends
and family to hear my rantings and ravings

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.080
about haunted animatronics.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:58.690
That happens
more frequently than you might think.

00:09:58.690 --> 00:10:01.660
I can even share my computer screen
to present my 87 part slide

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:03.579
deck about all the hidden lore
that I just found.

00:10:03.579 --> 00:10:05.209
And here's the kicker, friends, Meet

00:10:05.209 --> 00:10:09.130
isn't just for boring business meetings
or Theorist corporate mandated fun nights.

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:10.779
It also works
great for your everyday life.

00:10:10.779 --> 00:10:12.529
In fact,
I realized that I actually use Meet

00:10:12.529 --> 00:10:14.890
for more than you'd think
outside of work as well.

00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:16.779
And I'm not
talking about video calling the pizzeria

00:10:16.779 --> 00:10:18.339
to make sure that the bear and the fox
stay put.

00:10:18.339 --> 00:10:20.480
As someone who wants to keep in touch
with my parents,

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:22.529
and as a dad who wants my son
to have a close relationship

00:10:22.529 --> 00:10:24.860
with his grandparents,
Google Meet's incredible.

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:27.890
We wrangle Ollie and call up
my folks with super clear video

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:30.500
no matter where we are or what device
we're using.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:31.959
Sure it works on our computers and laptops,

00:10:31.959 --> 00:10:34.480
but Google Meet's
also available for tablets and phones.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:37.459
You even use it through a web
browser, no problem.

00:10:37.459 --> 00:10:38.480
Basically any modern device

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:41.519
with an OS is going to be able
to use Google Meet in some way or another.

00:10:41.519 --> 00:10:43.570
In fact,
if you happen to have an Android phone,

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:46.960
like basically every one on team Theorist
does, it already comes preinstalled

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:49.170
and integrated
into your contacts and messages.

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:52.399
And if you have an iPhone, it's super easy
to install from the App Store.

00:10:52.399 --> 00:10:54.639
So, please, do yourself a favor
and try Google Meet today

00:10:54.639 --> 00:10:56.590
by clicking the link in the description
below.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:59.020
The quality is incredible and
it's easy to use.

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:00.020
What more do you need?

00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:03.139
Again, go check out Google Meet by
clicking on the link in the description.

00:11:03.139 --> 00:11:05.860
One last big thank you to Google Meet
for sponsoring this portion of the video,

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:07.490
and now let's put back on our employee

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:11.180
uniforms and head back out to the pizzeria
to figure out what exactly is going on

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:12.360
in Five Nights at Freddy's.

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:14.139
So really
when we look at a lot of the clues

00:11:14.139 --> 00:11:17.089
coming from these trailers,
the story is largely what you'd expect.

00:11:17.089 --> 00:11:19.950
There's a string of children disappearing
from the pizzeria, resulting in Freddy

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:21.310
Fazbear's shutting down.

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:23.170
Judging from both the kids
drawing on the wall

00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:25.760
and this shot from the trailer,
it looks like Afton killed

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:28.800
five children, as we'd expect
from the lure of the first game.

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:31.410
Our favorite bunny-themed serial killer
hid the bodies of the kids

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:33.620
inside the animatronic suits,
and, in so doing,

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:35.620
trapped their souls
inside the robots forever.

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:38.100
And we know that they're sticking
with that specific part of the lore

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:39.809
based on the jump scare here.

00:11:42.452 --> 00:11:43.870
Oh, it is so good

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:45.150
every time I see it.

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:47.070
Children's hands
popping out of animatronic mouths,

00:11:47.070 --> 00:11:48.459
not only is it terrifying,

00:11:48.459 --> 00:11:51.360
it tells us that
he definitely hid the bodies inside there.

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:54.680
But now recently, people have been poking
around the old abandoned pizzeria.

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:58.270
As we see in the most recent trailer,
some smalltime criminals break in intent

00:11:58.270 --> 00:12:00.459
on robbing the place
and thrashing it up for fun.

00:12:00.459 --> 00:12:01.660
I believe that that sequence

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:03.430
is probably going
to be the beginning of the film,

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:06.010
these characters breaking in
before they're met with a terrible fate.

00:12:06.010 --> 00:12:09.019
The possessed animatronics come to life
and kill them as they're mid crime,

00:12:09.019 --> 00:12:10.550
not only showing the audience early on

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:13.550
that these things are terrifying,
but also creating a giant problem

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:14.550
for Afton,

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:17.579
who now risks having more people
poking around his old murder den.

00:12:17.579 --> 00:12:20.510
Hoping to prevent future break
ins and deeply uncomfortable questions

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:23.300
about his past,
Afton decides to hire a security guard

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:24.940
to keep an eye on the place
during the night.

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:27.560
His first option doesn't exactly work out
all that well.

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:28.710
But, not to be deterred,

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:31.550
our plucky mass murderer
tries and tries again

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:33.550
to find someone who will keep the building
safe.

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:36.450
Enter our main character of the movie,
Mike Schmidt.

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:38.140
Mike will do anything for cash.

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:39.699
Based on these two shots

00:12:39.699 --> 00:12:40.840
from the first trailer here,

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:44.370
we know that Mike has a history
of working as a security guard, but likely

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:48.370
he got carried away in a previous role,
resulting in him getting fired.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.370
Desperate for cash
and with no one willing to hire him,

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:53.490
Mike takes a job as the night shift
security guard at Freddy Fazbear's

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:55.280
bringing his sister Abby with him.

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:57.529
Seems like things aren't too strange
starting off.

00:12:57.529 --> 00:12:58.511
Though it's certainly creepy,

00:12:58.511 --> 00:13:00.529
they explore the pizzeria
without much of an issue,

00:13:00.529 --> 00:13:02.800
until, of course,
there's a knock at the front door.

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:06.170
Mike goes out and meets Vanessa,
a police officer with a strange interest

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:07.170
in the building.

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:09.618
In fact,
she seems to know a lot about Freddy's.

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:18.029
Looks like somebody
watched our complete timeline.

00:13:18.029 --> 00:13:21.680
Soon as creepy occurrences start happening
all across the pizzeria, Mike realizes

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:23.412
what he's gotten himself into.

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:28.019
And here's where the stakes get higher.

00:13:28.019 --> 00:13:31.199
Obviously, the animatronics are going
to pose a danger to both Mike and Vanessa,

00:13:31.199 --> 00:13:33.700
but their well-being isn't going to be
the only thing on the line

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:34.700
during this movie.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:36.610
Throughout the trailers,
we see shots of Abby

00:13:36.610 --> 00:13:39.839
going off to explore the pizzeria alone
and ultimately hiding from Foxy

00:13:39.839 --> 00:13:40.839
in the ball pit.

00:13:40.839 --> 00:13:42.199
Let's
just hope that she doesn't time travel.

00:13:42.199 --> 00:13:44.580
In all seriousness, though, somehow
Abby will befriend animatronics,

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:48.850
especially the leader, Golden Fredbear,
a character that you'll notice

00:13:48.850 --> 00:13:52.139
never appears anywhere
except for in shots with her.

00:13:52.139 --> 00:13:53.170
Why does she befriend them?

00:13:53.170 --> 00:13:57.096
Or rather, why do the animatronics
choose to befriend Abby? Well...

00:13:59.871 --> 00:14:01.190
Yep, the animatronics want to add

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:04.920
another member to their ranks, and
that is going to be the big driving factor

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:05.920
for this movie.

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:07.600
Mike and Vanessa are going to rush
to try to solve

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:10.639
the mystery of the kid's disappearance
and put their spirits to rest,

00:14:10.639 --> 00:14:12.530
hopefully
with plenty of time to save Abby.

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:13.530
The scenes where we see Mike

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:15.300
interacting with the kids
outside the pizzeria,

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:17.850
I believe that this is where
Mike is trying to put the pieces together

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:20.100
and is speaking to the spirits in
something like his dreams.

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:23.070
Of course,
William Afton does not want this to happen

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:25.810
and has to get himself
physically involved, disguising himself

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:28.800
in his old Spring Trap costume
and chasing Mike and Vanessa around

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:32.325
in an attempt to silence them in the big,
scary action set pieces.

00:14:32.325 --> 00:14:35.649
Afton will likely capture
and injure Vanessa at some point,

00:14:35.649 --> 00:14:38.590
considering that we see a yellow rabbit
hand grabbing Vanessa's neck here

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:41.209
and Mike sitting by Vanessa
in the hospital looking concerned.

00:14:41.209 --> 00:14:44.079
So that's the main set up
for what I see happening in the movie,

00:14:44.079 --> 00:14:45.529
But what about the big twist?

00:14:45.529 --> 00:14:47.910
There's always got to be some sort
of a big twist in FNAF.

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:50.800
Well, I believe that it comes
with the identity of some of the spirits.

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:52.920
You see,
we actually get a pretty good idea

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:56.690
of which spirits possess which animatronic
bodies from this shot in the trailers.

00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:59.630
It's pretty obviously telegraphed:
bunny ear kid is Bonnie, redhead

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:02.680
with pirate claw is
Foxy, the girl wearing all yellow is Chica,

00:15:02.680 --> 00:15:04.290
and the boy with the top hat as Freddy.

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:06.899
As for the last kid, though, well,
the obvious thought was that

00:15:06.899 --> 00:15:08.700
he was going to become
the mysterious Golden Freddy.

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:12.190
I think that's what I and everyone else
assumed when we saw that first trailer.

00:15:12.190 --> 00:15:13.570
But now I'm not so sure.

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:15.949
The fact that
this fifth child in the shot doesn't have

00:15:15.949 --> 00:15:19.740
a characteristic explicitly linking him to
an animatronic has to be intentional.

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:21.180
And I believe that it was the filmmakers

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:23.820
keeping things ambiguous
so we wouldn't guess their twist.

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:26.490
I suspect that the fifth kid here
isn't Golden Freddy.

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:28.829
Instead, I think it might be the cupcake.

00:15:28.829 --> 00:15:30.000
Yeah, I know. I get it.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.529
It sounds ridiculous,
but hear me out on this one.

00:15:32.529 --> 00:15:35.009
In the latest trailer,
we clearly see cupcake moving around

00:15:35.009 --> 00:15:37.560
independently
and attacking someone without Chica's help.

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:40.779
My initial gut thought to this, well,
that's kind of stupid, to be honest.

00:15:40.779 --> 00:15:44.620
Like, does Chica's soul transfer down
into the cupcake alone for remote attacks,

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:46.240
leaving Chica soulless for a while now?

00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:48.680
Or can a spirit divide itself
and act on different parts

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:49.940
of the character at different times?

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:51.336
You know what? I'm not sure.

00:15:51.336 --> 00:15:54.209
I don't have a good answer for it,
but I do think that this would open up

00:15:54.209 --> 00:15:57.680
an incredibly dark
and compelling twist on Golden Freddy.

00:15:57.680 --> 00:15:59.910
Remember these five kids
who disappeared at Freddy Fazbear's

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:03.040
in this shot aren't the only kids
that have gone missing in this story.

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:04.040
We still have ourselves

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:07.230
Mike's missing brother, Garrett,
who we talked about earlier is the kid

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:10.700
in the back of the car likely being carted
away by ol' Billy Afton up in front.

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:12.370
I mean, in this franchise,
it would be shocking

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:14.520
if someone kidnapping a child
wasn't William Afton.

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:16.250
Anyway,
why do we think that this is actually

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:18.470
the moment that we see
Mike's brother get kidnapped?

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:21.670
Well, again, we turn to actor
Lucas Grant and Instagram, where we see

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:25.230
this post of him hanging out with another
child actor named Wyatt Parker.

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:27.769
Parker, even calls Grant his "best bro,"

00:16:27.769 --> 00:16:28.769
an interesting choice of words

00:16:28.769 --> 00:16:29.769
considering that Parker

00:16:29.769 --> 00:16:34.519
was cast in the film as young Mike,
two twin brothers, one who gets kidnapped,

00:16:34.519 --> 00:16:37.850
almost a one-for-one replica of what we see
happen in the Silver Eyes novel.

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:40.230
So let me ask you:
what if Mike's brother is Golden Freddy

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:42.389
separate from the tragedy at the pizzeria?

00:16:42.389 --> 00:16:43.740
We can assume that Mike's brother

00:16:43.740 --> 00:16:46.120
was kidnapped in one of the earlier parts
of the timeline,

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:48.610
a time when Golden Freddy
would still be in use.

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:49.610
And in the games

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:53.910
we've long theorized that Mike Schmidt is,
in fact, Mike Afton, son of William Afton.

00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:54.910
This would also mean

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:57.319
that his little brother
was the crying child who was killed

00:16:57.319 --> 00:16:59.560
and became one of the spirits
that possessed Golden Freddy.

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:01.300
Given the fact that Mike's father
has been cast

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:03.639
and is distinctly
not being played by Matthew Lillard,

00:17:03.639 --> 00:17:06.299
I don't think that's the exact direction
that they're taking for the movie.

00:17:06.299 --> 00:17:09.260
But taking the core of that story,
keeping Mike's brother is Golden

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:12.049
Freddy, well
that would fit with both the timeline

00:17:12.049 --> 00:17:14.819
and serve as a devastating twist
to the casual audience.

00:17:14.819 --> 00:17:15.980
It would also explain why

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:18.900
Abby is spending so much time
with Golden Freddy in the trailers.

00:17:18.900 --> 00:17:19.990
It's her spending time with the brother

00:17:19.990 --> 00:17:23.030
that she never got to know
whether she realizes it or not.

00:17:23.030 --> 00:17:24.030
It could also explain why

00:17:24.030 --> 00:17:28.069
Golden Freddy retains blue eyes when
all the other animatronics have red ones.

00:17:28.069 --> 00:17:30.980
The circumstances of his possession
are just a little bit different

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.910
and he's interacting
with the family member.

00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:35.780
So, Afton attacks, Mike and Vanessa,
for getting too close to his secrets

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:38.299
and despite fighting back, they
ultimately lose.

00:17:38.299 --> 00:17:39.299
As they're about to die,

00:17:39.299 --> 00:17:42.940
Abby is able to win over the animatronics
and use them to fight back against Afton

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:44.010
saving them all.

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:47.270
You'll notice one of the oddities of
the trailer is the design of Spring Trap.

00:17:47.270 --> 00:17:49.059
It is different
from what we see in the games.

00:17:49.059 --> 00:17:50.059
It's cleaner and it's more

00:17:50.059 --> 00:17:51.059
put together.

00:17:51.059 --> 00:17:52.090
It has not gone through all the rotten

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:54.230
decay
that we'd expect from this character.

00:17:54.230 --> 00:17:56.340
I believe that's exactly how it ends.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:18:00.460
Mike, Abby, Vanessa and the animatronics
defeat Afton by trapping him in the walls,

00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:01.830
tying a bow on the end of this movie

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:04.330
while still leaving him in a position
to turn into the decayed,

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:07.400
rotten corpse that we all know
and love for the eventual sequel.

00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:09.750
However, all things can't end
happily here.

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:11.420
I believe there's a good chance
that the animatronics

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:14.510
are going to wind up getting
what they want out of Abby in the end.

00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:17.711
Her name is an anagram of baby,
after all, an animatronic

00:18:17.711 --> 00:18:19.710
that first appeared in FNAF:
Sister Location.

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:23.400
The team celebrates the defeat of Afton
only for Abby to accidentally stumble

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:26.870
into a clown outfit or maybe get
put there by a vengeful Golden Freddy

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:30.260
giving us our villain and the problem
to solve in the eventual second

00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:33.419
movie, saving the girl from her eternal,
ceaseless torment.

00:18:33.419 --> 00:18:36.960
Or maybe that ceaseless torment
is just meant for me, who is now tasked

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:41.070
with trying to solve the timeline of this
franchise across multiple channels.

00:18:41.070 --> 00:18:44.740
Truly, the animatronics have taken
another victim.

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:48.852
But hey, that's just a theory, a Film Theory.

00:18:48.852 --> 00:18:50.835
Aaaand cut...

